# v0.24.12 — Multi-key consensus live validation and single-proposer restoration

## P1 Phase 3 — Bridge multi-signature and Merkle enforcement live validation (2026-08-24)

- fix(bridge): add `bridge_state_root` to `BlockHeaderRequest`
  - `POST /rpc/bridge/block-headers` now carries the bridge event trie root so
    `store_block_header` can persist it and Merkle proof verification can succeed.
  - Without this field ingested headers had an empty bridge state root and
    `_validate_proof` rejected every real proof.

- fix(bridge): refresh `registered_at` when re-registering an existing bridge validator
  - `BridgeValidatorMixin.register_validator` now sets `existing.registered_at =
    datetime.now(UTC)` on re-registration.
  - Previously the validator-set freshness check treated re-registered sets as
    stale because the timestamp never advanced.

- ops(bridge): live activation of multi-signature and Merkle-proof enforcement
  - `/etc/aitbc/blockchain.env` on `hub.aitbc` and `aitbc3` set:
    - `BRIDGE_RELEASE_ENABLED=true` during validation, then `false`
    - `BRIDGE_MULTISIG_ENABLED=true`
    - `BRIDGE_REQUIRE_MERKLE_PROOF=true`
    - `BRIDGE_MULTISIG_THRESHOLD=2`
    - `BRIDGE_MULTISIG_VALIDATORS=2`
    - `BRIDGE_ADMIN_ADDRESSES=0xfe2d63fe87db282083b9159e5857cac788af9e03`
    - `BRIDGE_SUPPORTED_CHAINS=ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net,ait-shop-island.aitbc.bubuit.net`
  - Two bridge validators registered for `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net` on both nodes.

- live(bridge): end-to-end hub-to-island transfers with 2-of-2 multi-sig and Merkle proof
  - Lock 1 compute-second on `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net` to `ait-shop-island.aitbc.bubuit.net`.
  - Wait for the `BRIDGE_LOCK` transaction to be anchored in a hub block with a non-zero
    `bridge_state_root`.
  - Build a Merkle inclusion proof with `GET /rpc/bridge/transfer/{id}/proof`.
  - Store the hub block header on `aitbc3` with an admin-signed
    `POST /rpc/bridge/block-headers` request.
  - Confirm on `ait-shop-island` with `POST /rpc/bridge/confirm` using the confirmer
    signature, block proposer signature, validator attestation, and Merkle proof.
  - Verified the recipient balance increased on `ait-shop-island`.

- live(bridge): negative-case validation
  - Missing `merkle_proof` → `400 Invalid transfer proof`.
  - Insufficient validator signatures (proposer only, threshold 2) → `400 Invalid transfer proof`.
  - Invalid confirmer signature → `403 Invalid confirmer signature`.
  - Block-header ingestion with invalid admin signature → `403 Invalid or unauthorized bridge admin signature`.

- docs(bridge): updated `docs/releases/STATUS.md`, `docs/features/2-bridge-cross-chain.md`,
  and `docs/architecture/bridge-threat-model.md` with the live validation results,
  honest trust-custodian assessment, and the release-fence being returned to `false`.


